ou choose it\" /> **What the user does:** You choose the app as your default payment app, then tap a reader Answer a payment terminal as a virtual card (Android, once you pick it as d"],[323,"<Chips /> Can act as a contactless card or key when you pick it as default Lets an app act as a contactless card or key that other readers tap. A phone that emulates a card can hold payment, transit or access credentials without the OS wallet. Opening it to apps changes who controls tap to pay. <Reach level=\"3\" label=\"Ongoing once you choose it\" /> **What the user does:** You choose the app in Settings under Tap and pay, then tap a reader Answer readers with a stored card, ticket or key Hold pay"],[160,"<Chips /> Can act as your phone's password and passkey manager once you turn it on An app registers as the person's password and passkey manager for the whole system. The chosen manager can supply logins for every other app and site, and sees which services the person signs into. It is one of the most trusted roles on the phone. <Reach level=\"4\" label=\"Every login you store with it\" /> **What the user does:** You open Settings and choose this app as your passwords and passkeys provider Save pass"],[217,"<Chips /> Can add a Wi-Fi network to your phone, usually to set up a smart device Adds a Wi-Fi network to the phone, usually to onboard a smart device. Changes network state, so both OSes ask the person. Apple needs a capability and Android needs a normal permission. <Reach level=\"2\" label=\"One network, with your approval\" /> **What the user does:** You tap Connect or Set up device and approve the Wi-Fi join prompt Suggest or add a Wi-Fi network by name and password Join a device's setup Wi-Fi o"],[441,"<Chips /> Can add an ID to a link so the next site can recognize your visit Adding an ID to a link's URL so the next site can read it and link the visit. Meta adds fbclid to outbound clicks; Google's linker adds \\_gl with first party cookie IDs valid for a short time 