the same site | | Capability                    | Kind          | In one line                                                                             |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| enumerateDevices label gating | Gets silently | Can count your cameras, mics and speakers, but names stay hidden until you allow access | | Capability                                             | Kind           | In one line                                                                |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| HTML &lt;usermedia&gt; element (camera and microphone) | Asks you first | Can ask for camera or microphone through a button the browser draws itself | | Capability    | Kind                 | In one line                                                            |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| MediaRecorder | Works without asking | Can save a camera, mic or screen stream to a file, once you allowed it | | Capability                 | Kind           | In one line                                                               |\n| -------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Microphone (audio capture) | Asks you first | Can hear and record live audio from your microphone while the tab is open | | Capability                           | Kind                          | In one line                                              |\n| ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Picture-in-Picture and automatic PiP | Does something on your device | Can float a video in a small window over your other apps | | Capability                         | Kind                 | In one line                                                           |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Region Capture and Element Capture | Works without asking | Can crop a screen share to one part of the page, with no extra prompt | | Capability                     | Kind           | In one line                                                           |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Screen, window and tab capture | Asks you first | Can see the screen, window or tab you choose to share, until you stop | | Capability             | Kind           | In one line                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Web Speech recognition | Asks you first | Can turn your spoken words into text while you speak and the tab is open |"],[77,"Seeing, hearing and recording. 7 capabilities in this group. | Capability | Kind           | In one line                                                    |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Camera     | Asks you first | Can use your camera while the app is open, after you tap Allow | | Capability                       | Kind          | In one line                                               |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Camera and microphone indicators | Gets silently | Can't use the camera or mic without a dot or chip showing | | Capability                                     | Kind                 | In one line                                                                  |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Camera extensions and hardware camera controls | Works without asking | Can use phone camera modes such as night and HDR, after you allow the camera | | Capability                    | Kind                 | In one line                                                               |\n| ----------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Global camera and mic toggles | Works without asking | Can show you a blank camera and silence when you flip a phone wide switch | | Capability | Kind           | In one line                                                          |\n| ---------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Microphone | Asks you first | Can listen through your microphone while in use, after you tap Allow | | Capability              | Kind          | In one line                                                       |\n| ----------------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Recording indicator dot | Gets silently | Can't use the camera or mic without a green or orange dot showing | | Capability         | Kind           | In one line                                                  |\n| ------------------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Speech recognition | Asks you first | Can turn your speech into text, sometimes on Apple's servers |"],[155,"Steps, heart rate, workouts, health records. 7 capabilities in this group. | Capability   | Kind           | In one line                                                            |\n| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Body sensors | Asks you first | Can see your heart rate and similar body signals while the app is open | | Capability                 | Kind           | In one line                                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Body sensors in background | Asks you first | Can keep checking your heart rate and vitals while the app is not on screen | | Capability                     | Kind           | In one line                                                                       |\n| ------------------------------ | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Clinical health records (FHIR) | Asks you first | Can see your medical records, such as conditions and allergies, if you share them | | Capability                 | Kind           | In one line                                                                    |\n| -------------------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Health Connect permissions | Asks you first | Can see and add health data, one type at a time, from Health Connect or Health | | Capability                                 | Kind           | In one line                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------ | -------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Health data (HealthKit and Health Connect) | Asks you first | Can see and add health data such as steps and sleep, one type at a time | | Capability                                     | Kind          | In one line                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Health information (declared, not sensor data) | Gets silently | Can't use your health sensors in LinkedIn; health info is only on the store label | | Capability                 | Kind                 | In one line                                                                             |\n| -------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| SensorKit research sensors | Works without asking | Can't collect broad sensor data like research studies do, unless Apple approves a study |"],[889,"The best contributions are small: fix a fact, add a missing browser version, add a source, or write a new capability. You do not need to write code. You only edit JSON. Fork ever-just/platform-ontology on GitHub and clone your fork. Every capability page on this site ends with an **Edit this data on GitHub** link that opens the exact file. To add a new capability, create a file at `data/<space>/<group>/<slug>.json` where the slug is the id without its `mob.` or `web.` prefix. The easiest start is to copy a neighbor in the same group and change the values. Run the build in strict mode. It checks the schema, ids, folders, links between capabilities and the writing rules, and it stops with an error if anything is off. Push your branch and open a pull request. Say what you changed and add a source link for any new fact. A reviewer will check the facts, not your formatting. A stable `id` that starts with `mob.` or `web.` and matches the file name. A `kind` and `group` from the data model, and a folder that matches the group. Shared facts once at the top level. Per platform facts only under `platforms.android`, `platforms.ios` or `platforms.web`. `limits.can` and `limits.cannot` with 2 to 5 short items each, and a `reach` from 1 to 4. At least one entry in `refs`, with a link to official documentation or a spec, and an honest `confidence`. Links in `related` and `web_equivalents` that point to ids that exist. Plain language is the point of this project. Write for someone who has never read a spec. Use short sentences and everyday words. Explain a term the first time you use it. Say what a person sees and what an app can do, not how the API is shaped. **Never use em dashes or en dashes.** Rewrite the sentence with a period, comma, colon or parentheses. Write ranges as \"7 to 15\". The build rejects dashes in data files. Use an ordinary hyphen only inside a real compound word, such as \"one-click\". Keep each item in `can` and `cannot` to one idea. Be neutral about abuse. Describe what is possible and what was reported, with a source. Do not copy long text from other sources. Summarize and link. Not ready to edit? Open an issue with the capability id, what is wrong and a source if you have one."],[892,"The data is plain files in a Git repository. Nothing hides behind a database, so every change is a normal pull request that anyone can read. <Card title=\"One file per capability\">Small files make reviews easy and merge conflicts rare.</Card> <Card title=\"Folders carry meaning\">The path tells you the space and the group before you open the file.</Card> <Card title=\"Shared once, different per platform\">A concept is never duplicated across operating systems.</Card> <Card title=\"Bundles are built\">A build step validates everything and writes ready to use JSON.</Card> Every capability lives in its own file: `space` is `mobile` or `web`. `group` is a key from `data/taxonomy.json`, for example `camera-mic-screen`. `slug` is the `id` without its `mob.` or `web.` prefix. The id `web.camera.camera-ptz` is stored as `data/web/camera-mic-screen/camera.camera-ptz.json`. The build checks that the folder, the `space` field and the `group` field agree, so a file can never sit in the wrong place. A native capability such as precise location is one idea on Android and iPhone. Its name, meaning, data fields, limits and history are stored **once**, at the top level of the file. Only what truly differs sits in per platform blocks: This is a simplified example: Web capabilities keep one support record per browser under `platforms.web.support`. A native capability and its web twin are connected with `web_equivalents`. Labels, icons and descriptions for kinds, groups, lifecycle stages and browsers live in `data/taxonomy.json`. Renaming a label never touches the 844 capability files. `scripts/build-data.mjs` reads every file, validates it, and writes `dist/`: | Output               | What it is                    |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `dist/ontology.json` | Everything, plus the taxonomy | | Output            | What it is                               |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `dist/index.json` | A light list for search boxes and tables | | Output               | What it is              |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `dist/taxonomy.json` | Labels and descriptions | | Output                       | What it is                                                            |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dist/platform/android.json` | Native capabilities with the Android block flattened under `platform` | | Output                   | What it is                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dist/platform/ios.json` | Native capabilities with the iPhone block flattened under `platform` | | Output                   | What it is                                             |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `dist/platform/web.json` | Web capabilities with browser support under `platform` | The website serves them under `/data/`. See Getting started for the URLs. The build also checks that ids are unique, that every `related` and `web_equivalents` link points to a real capability, that groups and kinds exist, and that no text contains an em or en dash. Run it with `STRICT=1` and any problem stops the build with a non zero exit code. `schema/capability.schema.json` describes one capability. Point your editor at it to get completion and live errors while you edit a file: This site is generated from the same files. A script reads each JSON file and writes one page per capability, so the docs can never drift from the data. Every page ends with a link back to the file on GitHub."],[895,"The map covers three platforms. Native apps are described once for Android and iPhone together. Websites are described once with support for 7 browsers. <Card title=\"Android\" href=\"/docs/capabilities/mobile/\">361 capabilities. Permissions, protection levels, API levels, Settings paths and Play policy.</Card> <Card title=\"iPhone (iOS)\" href=\"/docs/capabilities/mobile/\">361 capabilities. Info.plist keys, entitlements, prompts, Settings paths and App Store policy.</Card> <Card title=\"Web browsers\" href=\"/docs/capabilities/web/\">483 capabilities. Support in Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari, Safari on iPhone, Chrome on Android and Samsung Internet.</Card> | Kind                          | What it means             | Android and iPhone | Web |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ | --- |\n| Asks you first (`permission`) | A pop up asks for your OK | 66                 | 55  | | Kind                              | What it means              | Android and iPhone | Web |\n| --------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------ | --- |\n| You pick what to share (`picker`) | You choose the exact items | 6                  | 7   | | Kind                                | What it means                   | Android and iPhone | Web |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------